# Per-operator scratch: never the deliverable
AISessions/*
!AISessions/README.md

# Local-only Claude Code settings (per-machine permission approvals, etc.): never published.
# The globs catch every variant/nesting, so an auto-approved command can't leak through this file.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
**/settings.local.json

# Claude Code runtime artifacts (live session locks): machine state, never published.
.claude/*.lock

# OS / editor / backup noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
._*
.___*
*.bak
*.tmp
*~

# Per-customer project content (Sites/) IS tracked: the actual project work is what gets versioned.
# This PUBLIC template ships one example site (Sites/Example-HighlandWTP). Once you start committing
# YOUR real customer sites into your clone/fork, keep that repository PRIVATE / access-controlled.

# FrameworX per-solution LOCAL / TRANSIENT state: version the solution + its diffable Git/ export,
# NOT machine/session working state (this is the "position saving / profile" data):
# Designer<->MCP session logs
**/DesignerData/**/MCP/
# compiled-script build output (regenerated on every build)
**/DesignerData/**/NetCompiler/
# Designer-regenerated tag cross-reference caches
**/DesignerData/**/TagsUsage/
# window & panel positions (per-user UI state)
**/DesignerData/**/Settings/Designer-UIState.settings.json
# Xceed DataGrid column/UI caches (per-user)
**/DesignerData/**/Settings/*.table.xml
# last-selected execution profile (per-user)
**/DesignerData/**/Settings/Designer-InitialProfile.settings.json
# debugger breakpoints / watch variables (per-user)
**/DesignerData/**/Settings/Debugger-*.bin
# Designer's own deleted-file backups
**/DesignerData/**/Git/backup/
# timestamped solution backups & deleted-file markers
*.backup
*.deleted

# FrameworX runtime-generated databases (alarms/historian/retentive/users/business):
# regenerated at run time, never version them
*.dbAlarm
*.dbHistorian
*.dbRetentive
*.dbRuntimeUsers
*.dbBusiness

# SQLite sidecars (live Designer session state, never commit)
*.dbsln-shm
*.dbsln-wal

# Per-project test-run output: regenerated on every run of the run-tests gate.
# (Templates/Examples/Brewery/results/ stays tracked: it is committed reference evidence.)
Sites/*/Tests/results/

# Python noise (run-tests checker, invariant linter)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
